2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“hepatic resection” means the surgical removal of a part of the liver;
“liver — post hepatic resection (donor)” refers to the absence of a part of the liver in a person due to having undergone hepatic resection for the purpose of transplantation of a part of his liver into the body of another living person;
“patient” means a person to whom a notification referred to in regulation 3 relates;
“recipient” means the person into whose body a part of the patient’s liver is or will be transplanted.

3. For the purposes of section 6(1) of the Act, a notification by the manager of a healthcare institution to the Registrar that a person has undergone hepatic resection for the purpose of transplantation into the body of another living person or is undergoing any treatment for liver — post hepatic resection (donor), at the healthcare institution shall —
(a)contain, in relation to that patient, the information specified in the First Schedule;
(b)be made in any of the Forms set out in the Second Schedule or at the Registry’s Internet website at http://www.nrdo.gov.sg;
(c)be sent to the Registrar —
(i)by hand (including by courier);
(ii)by registered mail; or
(iii)by using such secure electronic notification system as may be approved by the Registrar; and
(d)be made within the following time:
(i)where the patient has undergone hepatic resection, not later than 3 months after hepatic resection; or
(ii)where the patient is undergoing treatment for liver — post hepatic resection (donor) in the healthcare institution, not later than 3 months after the first of such treatments received by the patient at that healthcare institution on or after 1st November 2009.

THIRD SCHEDULE
Regulation 4
Additional Information for New Cases
1. Particulars of patient for new case registration:
(a)citizenship or resident status;
(b)gender;
(c)ethnic group;
(d)marital status;
(e)country of birth;
(f)educational level;
(g)employment status;
(h)relationship to recipient.
2. Particulars of recipient:
(a)name;
(b)identification number (including NRIC number, passport number, Foreign Identification Number or hospital registration number);
(c)date of birth or age (if date of birth is unknown);
(d)citizenship or resident status;
(e)gender;
(f)ethnic group;
(g)marital status;
(h)name of recipient’s healthcare institution.
3. Patient baseline information (pre-donation):
(a)date of baseline information;
(b)weight;
(c)height;
(d)smoking status;
(e)EQ-5D (including mobility, self-care, usual activities, pain or discomfort and anxiety or depression);
(f)liver panel (including date);
(g)full blood count (including date);
(h)prothrombin time (PT) (including date);
(i)ultrasound, CT scan or MRI (including findings and date).
4. Data related to donor hepatic resection:
(a)place of surgery;
(b)type of hepatic resection;
(c)complications during hospitalisation (including type(s), and date if the donor has liver failure or impairment);
(d)date of initial discharge;
(e)live donor discharge disposition.
5. Details of notifying healthcare institution:
person who made the notification.

FOURTH SCHEDULE
Regulation 4
Additional Information for Cases
Undergoing Treatment
1. Patient’s status (at follow-up):
(a)date of consultation;
(b)healthcare institution (including specific centre, department or clinic) responsible for subsequent treatment or follow-up;
(c)weight;
(d)height;
(e)smoking status;
(f)employment status;
(g)EQ-5D (including mobility, self-care, usual activities, pain or discomfort and anxiety or depression);
(h)other illnesses since last visit (including diagnosis and date of diagnosis);
(i)admission to hospital since last visit (including diagnosis and date of admission).
2. Investigations (at follow-up):
(a)liver panel (including date);
(b)full blood count (including date);
(c)prothrombin time (PT) (including date);
(d)ultrasound, CT Scan or MRI (including date and findings);
(e)ERCP or MRCP (including date and findings).
3. Adverse condition relating to liver:
whether or not the patient has liver failure (including date, cause of liver failure, on transplant waiting list and reason for not on transplant waiting list).
4. Vital status:
(a) whether patient is living or deceased;
(b)where the patient is deceased, the date, place and cause of death.
5. Details of notifying healthcare institution:
person who made the notification.
